<title>KijaniSpace Node Wiring</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Sans+Condensed:wght@600;700&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap">

<style>
  :root {
    --bg:        #F6F9FA;
    --surface:   #FFFFFF;
    --surface-2: #EBF1F3;
    --border:    #D2DEE3;
    --border-2:  #B9CAD1;
    --ink:       #15242A;
    --ink-2:     #485D67;
    --ink-3:     #7B9099;
    --rail12:    #B45F09;
    --rail33:    #0D6E88;
    --data:      #6D3BD1;
    --note-bg:   #FBF3E6;
    --note-bd:   #E3C79C;
    --danger:    #A32C24;
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
      --bg:        #0D1517;
      --surface:   #162226;
      --surface-2: #1D2C31;
      --border:    #2B3F46;
      --border-2:  #3D555E;
      --ink:       #E3ECEF;
      --ink-2:     #A2B6BE;
      --ink-3:     #728A93;
      --rail12:    #EFA243;
      --rail33:    #46B7D2;
      --data:      #A98CF7;
      --note-bg:   #221B10;
      --note-bd:   #47381E;
      --danger:    #F08A80;
    }
  }

  :root[data-theme="dark"] {
    --bg:        #0D1517;
    --surface:   #162226;
    --surface-2: #1D2C31;
    --border:    #2B3F46;
    --border-2:  #3D555E;
    --ink:       #E3ECEF;
    --ink-2:     #A2B6BE;
    --ink-3:     #728A93;
    --rail12:    #EFA243;
    --rail33:    #46B7D2;
    --data:      #A98CF7;
    --note-bg:   #221B10;
    --note-bd:   #47381E;
    --danger:    #F08A80;
  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: "IBM Plex Sans", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }

  .sheet {
    max-width: 1080px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 40px 24px 80px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 44px;
  }

  /* ---- title block, like the corner of an engineering drawing ---- */
  .titleblock {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: 20px;
    padding: 22px 24px;
    align-items: end;
  }
  .titleblock h1 {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Sans Condensed", "IBM Plex Sans", sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 4vw, 2.4rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0 0 6px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .titleblock p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 62ch; }
  .meta {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    text-align: right;
    line-height: 1.8;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .meta b { color: var(--ink-2); font-weight: 500; }

  h2 {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Sans Condensed", "IBM Plex Sans", sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.45rem;
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }
  h2 .num {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    display: block;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
  }
  h3 {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Sans Condensed", "IBM Plex Sans", sans-serif;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  section > p { margin: 0 0 16px; max-width: 68ch; color: var(--ink-2); }
  section > p strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }

  figure {
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: 20px 20px 0;
  }
  .canvas { overflow-x: auto; }
  figure svg {
    display: block;
    min-width: 640px;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  figcaption {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    padding: 14px 2px 18px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin-top: 16px;
    max-width: 78ch;
  }
  figcaption b { color: var(--ink-2); font-weight: 500; }

  /* ---- legend ---- */
  .legend {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px 22px;
    padding: 12px 0 0;
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .legend span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; }
  .swatch { width: 20px; height: 0; border-top-width: 3px; border-top-style: solid; }
  .sw12 { border-color: var(--rail12); }
  .sw33 { border-color: var(--rail33); }
  .swd  { border-color: var(--data); }
  .swg  { border-color: var(--ink-3); }
  .swsh { border-top-style: dashed; border-color: var(--ink-3); }

  /* ---- tables ---- */
  .tablewrap { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--surface); }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; min-width: 560px; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 10px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); vertical-align: top; }
  thead th {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Sans Condensed", sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    background: var(--surface-2);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  code, .mono {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.86em;
  }
  td code { background: var(--surface-2); padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 2px; white-space: nowrap; }
  .pin { color: var(--rail33); font-weight: 500; }

  /* ---- callouts ---- */
  .note {
    border: 1px solid var(--note-bd);
    background: var(--note-bg);
    padding: 16px 18px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .note h3 { margin: 0; }
  .note p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 74ch; }
  .note p strong { color: var(--ink); }

  ul.checks { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  ul.checks li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 26px 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    max-width: 76ch;
  }
  ul.checks .n {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    padding-top: 3px;
  }
  ul.checks strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }

  hr { border: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin: 0; }
</style>

<div class="sheet">

  <header class="titleblock">
    <div>
      <h1>Water Sensor Node — Wiring</h1>
      <p>Assembly reference for the KijaniSpace LoRaWAN water-quality station: five probes across
         three buses, one power-gated 12 V rail, WaziSenseV2 controller.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="meta">
      SITE&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Lake Victoria / fish farm</b><br>
      MCU&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>WaziSenseV2 (ATmega328P)</b><br>
      RADIO&nbsp;<b>SX1272 · EU868 · SF12</b><br>
      SKETCH&nbsp;<b>WaterSensorNode.ino</b>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <section>
    <h2><span class="num">DRAWING 01</span>System overview</h2>
    <p>The node splits into two voltage domains. Everything the MCU talks to directly runs at
       <strong>3.3 V</strong>; the two RS485 probes need <strong>10–30 V</strong> and are fed from a boosted
       12 V rail that a GPIO switches off between measurements. The RS485 bus and the I²C bus are
       independent — a fault on one does not take the other down.</p>

    <figure>
      <div class="canvas">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 600" role="img"
             aria-label="Block diagram: solar and battery feed a protection stage, which powers the WaziSense board at 3.3 volts and a boost converter to a gated 12 volt rail. The board drives an I2C bus to two Atlas EZO circuits, an RS485 bus through a MAX3485 transceiver to two Modbus probes, and a MAX31865 front-end on SPI for the three-wire PT1000.">
          <defs>
            <marker id="ar" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="currentColor"/>
            </marker>
            <marker id="ar12" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="var(--rail12)"/>
            </marker>
            <marker id="ard" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="var(--data)"/>
            </marker>
          </defs>

          <g font-family="IBM Plex Mono, monospace" font-size="12" fill="currentColor">

            <!-- ============ POWER ROW ============ -->
            <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none">
              <rect x="16"  y="30" width="126" height="52" rx="2"/>
              <rect x="196" y="30" width="126" height="52" rx="2"/>
              <rect x="376" y="30" width="126" height="52" rx="2"/>
              <rect x="556" y="30" width="126" height="52" rx="2"/>
            </g>
            <text x="79"  y="52" text-anchor="middle">Solar panel</text>
            <text x="79"  y="68" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)">6 V · 5–10 W</text>
            <text x="259" y="52" text-anchor="middle">Charge ctrl</text>
            <text x="259" y="68" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)">MPPT</text>
            <text x="439" y="52" text-anchor="middle">Battery</text>
            <text x="439" y="68" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)">18650 1–2× ∥</text>
            <text x="619" y="52" text-anchor="middle">Protection</text>
            <text x="619" y="68" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)">PTC · SS34 · TVS</text>

            <!-- power row arrows -->
            <g stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#ar12)">
              <line x1="142" y1="56" x2="190" y2="56"/>
              <line x1="322" y1="56" x2="370" y2="56"/>
              <line x1="502" y1="56" x2="550" y2="56"/>
            </g>

            <!-- split from protection -->
            <path d="M 682 56 L 730 56" stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/>
            <path d="M 730 56 L 730 118" stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="2" fill="none" marker-end="url(#ar12)"/>
            <path d="M 619 82 L 619 250 L 300 250" stroke="var(--rail33)" stroke-width="2" fill="none" marker-end="url(#ar)" color="var(--rail33)"/>
            <text x="470" y="242" fill="var(--rail33)">3.7 V → board VIN</text>

            <!-- boost + gate -->
            <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none">
              <rect x="666" y="122" width="128" height="50" rx="2"/>
              <rect x="666" y="200" width="128" height="50" rx="2"/>
            </g>
            <text x="730" y="143" text-anchor="middle">XL6009 boost</text>
            <text x="730" y="159" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)">3.7 V → 12 V</text>
            <text x="730" y="221" text-anchor="middle">High-side switch</text>
            <text x="730" y="237" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)">Pololu #2811</text>
            <line x1="730" y1="172" x2="730" y2="196" stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#ar12)"/>

            <!-- gate control from board -->
            <path d="M 300 300 L 620 300 L 620 225 L 662 225" stroke="var(--rail33)" stroke-width="1.6"
                  stroke-dasharray="5 4" fill="none" marker-end="url(#ar)" color="var(--rail33)"/>
            <text x="400" y="292" fill="var(--rail33)">D6 · rail enable</text>

            <!-- 12 V bus bar -->
            <line x1="730" y1="250" x2="730" y2="330" stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <line x1="470" y1="330" x2="960" y2="330" stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="3"/>
            <text x="836" y="322" fill="var(--rail12)">+12 V switched rail</text>
            <!-- bulk cap on the rail -->
            <g stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="2">
              <line x1="660" y1="330" x2="660" y2="352"/>
              <line x1="648" y1="352" x2="672" y2="352"/>
              <line x1="648" y1="359" x2="672" y2="359"/>
            </g>
            <text x="676" y="364" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">1000 µF</text>

            <!-- ============ BOARD ============ -->
            <rect x="16" y="262" width="284" height="222" rx="2" fill="var(--surface-2)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="32" y="288" font-family="IBM Plex Sans Condensed, sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="700" fill="var(--ink)">WaziSenseV2</text>
            <text x="32" y="305" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">ATmega328P · 3.3 V logic</text>
            <line x1="16" y1="316" x2="300" y2="316" stroke="var(--border-2)" stroke-width="1"/>

            <text x="32" y="340" fill="var(--rail33)">A4 SDA   A5 SCL</text>
            <text x="32" y="360" fill="var(--data)">D3 RX   D4 TX   D5 DE</text>
            <text x="32" y="380" fill="currentColor">A1 RTD-CS   D11/12/13 SPI</text>
            <text x="32" y="400" fill="currentColor">D6 rail EN   D8 LED   A0 VBAT</text>

            <line x1="16" y1="414" x2="300" y2="414" stroke="var(--border-2)" stroke-width="1"/>
            <text x="32" y="438">SX1272 radio</text>
            <text x="32" y="456" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">EU868 · SF12 · ABP</text>
            <!-- antenna -->
            <line x1="230" y1="446" x2="272" y2="446" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <path d="M 272 434 L 272 458" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <path d="M 278 438 L 278 454" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <path d="M 284 442 L 284 450" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <text x="216" y="472" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">λ/2 dipole</text>

            <!-- ============ I2C BRANCH ============ -->
            <path d="M 300 340 L 356 340" stroke="var(--rail33)" stroke-width="2" fill="none" marker-end="url(#ar)" color="var(--rail33)"/>
            <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none">
              <rect x="360" y="392" width="126" height="46" rx="2"/>
              <rect x="360" y="448" width="126" height="46" rx="2"/>
            </g>
            <path d="M 356 340 L 356 415 L 356 471" stroke="var(--rail33)" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/>
            <path d="M 356 415 L 356 415" stroke="var(--rail33)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <line x1="356" y1="415" x2="360" y2="415" stroke="var(--rail33)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <line x1="356" y1="471" x2="360" y2="471" stroke="var(--rail33)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <text x="423" y="411" text-anchor="middle">EZO-pH</text>
            <text x="423" y="428" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">I²C 0x63</text>
            <text x="423" y="467" text-anchor="middle">EZO-EC</text>
            <text x="423" y="484" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">I²C 0x64</text>
            <text x="304" y="356" fill="var(--rail33)" font-size="11">I²C</text>

            <!-- BNC probes -->
            <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none">
              <rect x="536" y="392" width="112" height="46" rx="2" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/>
              <rect x="536" y="448" width="112" height="46" rx="2" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/>
            </g>
            <line x1="486" y1="415" x2="532" y2="415" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
            <line x1="486" y1="471" x2="532" y2="471" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
            <text x="592" y="411" text-anchor="middle">pH probe</text>
            <text x="592" y="428" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">BNC</text>
            <text x="592" y="467" text-anchor="middle">EC probe K1.0</text>
            <text x="592" y="484" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">BNC</text>

            <!-- ============ RS485 BRANCH ============ -->
            <path d="M 300 360 L 356 360" stroke="var(--data)" stroke-width="2" fill="none" marker-end="url(#ard)"/>
            <rect x="360" y="336" width="110" height="48" rx="2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none"/>
            <text x="415" y="356" text-anchor="middle">MAX3485</text>
            <text x="415" y="372" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">3.3 V transceiver</text>

            <!-- A/B pair going right -->
            <line x1="470" y1="352" x2="960" y2="352" stroke="var(--data)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <line x1="470" y1="360" x2="960" y2="360" stroke="var(--data)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <text x="700" y="378" fill="var(--data)" font-size="11">RS485 A / B — Modbus-RTU 9600 8N1</text>

            <!-- three slaves -->
            <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none">
              <rect x="700" y="392" width="126" height="46" rx="2"/>
              <rect x="700" y="448" width="126" height="46" rx="2"/>
              <rect x="700" y="504" width="126" height="46" rx="2"/>
            </g>
            <g stroke="var(--data)" stroke-width="1.6">
              <line x1="740" y1="360" x2="740" y2="392"/>
              <line x1="740" y1="438" x2="740" y2="448"/>
            </g>
            <g stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="1.6">
              <line x1="800" y1="330" x2="800" y2="392"/>
              <line x1="800" y1="438" x2="800" y2="448"/>
            </g>
            <text x="763" y="411" text-anchor="middle">DO SEN0680</text>
            <text x="763" y="428" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">0x02 · 10–30 V</text>
            <text x="763" y="467" text-anchor="middle">Y511-A turbidity</text>
            <text x="763" y="484" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">0x03 · 5–12 V · wiper</text>

            <!-- PT1000 is NOT on the RS485 bus: bare RTD via MAX31865 on SPI -->
            <rect x="360" y="504" width="126" height="46" rx="2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none"/>
            <text x="423" y="523" text-anchor="middle">MAX31865</text>
            <text x="423" y="540" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">SPI · CS = A1</text>
            <path d="M 300 400 L 330 400 L 330 527 L 356 527" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <text x="336" y="470" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">SPI</text>
            <line x1="486" y1="527" x2="696" y2="527" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <text x="763" y="523" text-anchor="middle">PT1000 RTD</text>
            <text x="763" y="540" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">3-wire · 2×red + 1×white</text>

            <!-- ============ COMMON GROUND ============ -->
            <line x1="16" y1="576" x2="960" y2="576" stroke="var(--ink-3)" stroke-width="3"/>
            <g stroke="var(--ink-3)" stroke-width="1.4">
              <line x1="158" y1="484" x2="158" y2="576"/>
              <line x1="423" y1="494" x2="423" y2="576"/>
              <line x1="763" y1="550" x2="763" y2="576"/>
              <line x1="619" y1="82"  x2="619" y2="96"/>
            </g>
            <text x="24" y="568" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">GND — one continuous rail, never switched</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="legend">
        <span><i class="swatch sw12"></i>+12 V switched</span>
        <span><i class="swatch sw33"></i>3.3 V / logic</span>
        <span><i class="swatch swd"></i>data (RS485, I²C)</span>
        <span><i class="swatch swg"></i>GND</span>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        The GPIO on <b>D4</b> gates the +12 V rail only — the ground rail runs unbroken from the battery
        to every probe. Breaking ground instead would destroy the RS485 common reference and the bus
        would stop working. The RS485 slaves each carry a distinct Modbus address; the two Atlas EZO
        circuits sit at distinct I²C addresses.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <section>
    <h2><span class="num">DRAWING 02</span>RS485 bus detail</h2>
    <p>Both Modbus probes share one half-duplex pair. The MCU has a single hardware UART (taken by
       the USB debug console), so the bus runs on <code>SoftwareSerial</code> — pins
       <span class="mono pin">D3/D4</span> for data and <span class="mono pin">D5</span> tied to both
       <code>DE</code> and <code>RE</code> for direction. <strong>One 120 Ω terminator only, at the transceiver</strong>
       — see the calculation below for why a second one is wrong on this bus.</p>

    <figure>
      <div class="canvas">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 460" role="img"
             aria-label="RS485 wiring detail: MAX3485 transceiver pins RO, DI, DE and RE connect to board pins D3, D4 and D5. The A and B lines run as a shielded twisted pair with a single 120 ohm termination resistor at the transceiver end, fail-safe bias resistors of 680 ohms to 3.3 volts and ground, and two Modbus slaves tapped along the pair. The far end of the pair is left unterminated. The cable shield is grounded at the enclosure end only.">
          <defs>
            <marker id="ar2" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="currentColor"/>
            </marker>
          </defs>

          <g font-family="IBM Plex Mono, monospace" font-size="12" fill="currentColor">

            <!-- MCU stub -->
            <rect x="16" y="120" width="120" height="130" rx="2" fill="var(--surface-2)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="76" y="146" text-anchor="middle" font-family="IBM Plex Sans Condensed, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="var(--ink)">WaziSense</text>
            <text x="126" y="176" text-anchor="end" fill="var(--rail33)">D3</text>
            <text x="126" y="200" text-anchor="end" fill="var(--rail33)">D4</text>
            <text x="126" y="224" text-anchor="end" fill="var(--rail33)">D5</text>

            <!-- transceiver -->
            <rect x="230" y="112" width="150" height="150" rx="2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" fill="none"/>
            <text x="305" y="136" text-anchor="middle" font-family="IBM Plex Sans Condensed, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="var(--ink)">MAX3485</text>
            <text x="242" y="176">RO</text>
            <text x="242" y="200">DI</text>
            <text x="242" y="224">DE</text>
            <text x="242" y="244">RE</text>
            <text x="368" y="176" text-anchor="end">A</text>
            <text x="368" y="224" text-anchor="end">B</text>

            <!-- MCU <-> transceiver -->
            <g stroke="var(--rail33)" stroke-width="1.8">
              <line x1="136" y1="172" x2="236" y2="172"/>
              <line x1="136" y1="196" x2="236" y2="196"/>
              <line x1="136" y1="220" x2="216" y2="220"/>
              <line x1="216" y1="220" x2="216" y2="240"/>
              <line x1="216" y1="220" x2="236" y2="220"/>
              <line x1="216" y1="240" x2="236" y2="240"/>
            </g>
            <text x="150" y="164" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">RX</text>
            <text x="150" y="188" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">TX</text>
            <text x="140" y="258" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">DE + RE tied</text>

            <!-- VCC to transceiver -->
            <line x1="305" y1="112" x2="305" y2="76" stroke="var(--rail33)" stroke-width="1.8"/>
            <line x1="240" y1="76" x2="305" y2="76" stroke="var(--rail33)" stroke-width="1.8"/>
            <text x="236" y="72" text-anchor="end" fill="var(--rail33)">+3.3 V</text>

            <!-- A/B pair -->
            <line x1="380" y1="172" x2="930" y2="172" stroke="var(--data)" stroke-width="2.2"/>
            <line x1="380" y1="220" x2="930" y2="220" stroke="var(--data)" stroke-width="2.2"/>
            <text x="600" y="140" fill="var(--data)" font-size="11">A  —  shielded twisted pair</text>
            <text x="600" y="244" fill="var(--data)" font-size="11">B</text>

            <!-- shield: dashed, grounded one end only -->
            <path d="M 400 258 L 900 258" stroke="var(--ink-3)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="6 5" fill="none"/>
            <line x1="400" y1="258" x2="400" y2="392" stroke="var(--ink-3)" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <circle cx="900" cy="258" r="4" fill="none" stroke="var(--ink-3)" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <text x="906" y="262" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">open — do NOT ground far end</text>
            <text x="406" y="284" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">shield grounded at enclosure only</text>

            <!-- near-end 120R termination -->
            <rect x="398" y="184" width="26" height="24" rx="2" stroke="var(--data)" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none"/>
            <line x1="411" y1="172" x2="411" y2="184" stroke="var(--data)" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <line x1="411" y1="208" x2="411" y2="220" stroke="var(--data)" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <text x="430" y="200" fill="var(--data)" font-size="11">120 Ω</text>

            <!-- far end: deliberately NOT terminated -->
            <circle cx="930" cy="172" r="4" fill="none" stroke="var(--data)" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <circle cx="930" cy="220" r="4" fill="none" stroke="var(--data)" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <text x="930" y="152" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">no terminator here</text>
            <text x="930" y="140" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">(see note)</text>

            <!-- fail-safe bias -->
            <rect x="487" y="88" width="26" height="24" rx="2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" fill="none"/>
            <line x1="500" y1="112" x2="500" y2="172" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <line x1="500" y1="88"  x2="500" y2="76"  stroke="var(--rail33)" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <line x1="500" y1="76"  x2="560" y2="76"  stroke="var(--rail33)" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <text x="566" y="80" fill="var(--rail33)" font-size="11">+3.3 V</text>
            <text x="519" y="105" font-size="11">680 Ω</text>

            <rect x="487" y="292" width="26" height="24" rx="2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" fill="none"/>
            <line x1="500" y1="220" x2="500" y2="292" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <line x1="500" y1="316" x2="500" y2="392" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <text x="519" y="309" font-size="11">680 Ω</text>
            <text x="519" y="286" font-size="11" fill="var(--ink-3)">fail-safe bias</text>

            <!-- three slaves tapping the pair -->
            <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none">
              <rect x="600" y="316" width="112" height="44" rx="2"/>
              <rect x="740" y="316" width="112" height="44" rx="2"/>
              <rect x="600" y="316" width="112" height="44" rx="2"/>
            </g>
            <g stroke="var(--data)" stroke-width="1.6">
              <line x1="630" y1="172" x2="630" y2="316"/>
              <line x1="646" y1="220" x2="646" y2="316"/>
              <line x1="770" y1="172" x2="770" y2="316"/>
              <line x1="786" y1="220" x2="786" y2="316"/>
            </g>
            <text x="656" y="336" text-anchor="middle">probe n</text>
            <text x="656" y="352" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">A B GND +12 V</text>
            <text x="796" y="336" text-anchor="middle">probe n+1</text>
            <text x="796" y="352" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">A B GND +12 V</text>

            <!-- 12V feed to slaves -->
            <line x1="600" y1="424" x2="860" y2="424" stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="2.4"/>
            <g stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="1.6">
              <line x1="700" y1="360" x2="700" y2="424"/>
              <line x1="840" y1="360" x2="840" y2="424"/>
            </g>
            <text x="606" y="444" fill="var(--rail12)" font-size="11">+12 V switched rail (from D6 gate)</text>

            <!-- ground rail -->
            <line x1="16" y1="392" x2="930" y2="392" stroke="var(--ink-3)" stroke-width="2.6"/>
            <g stroke="var(--ink-3)" stroke-width="1.4">
              <line x1="76"  y1="250" x2="76"  y2="392"/>
              <line x1="305" y1="262" x2="305" y2="392"/>
              <line x1="672" y1="360" x2="672" y2="392"/>
              <line x1="812" y1="360" x2="812" y2="392"/>
            </g>
            <text x="24" y="384" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">GND</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="legend">
        <span><i class="swatch sw12"></i>+12 V switched</span>
        <span><i class="swatch sw33"></i>3.3 V / logic</span>
        <span><i class="swatch swd"></i>RS485 A / B</span>
        <span><i class="swatch swg"></i>GND</span>
        <span><i class="swatch swsh"></i>cable shield</span>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <b>One 120 Ω</b> resistor across A/B at the transceiver. The far end of the cable is left
        <b>unterminated</b>. The <b>680 Ω</b> fail-safe bias pair holds the idle bus at a defined level so
        noise is not decoded as data; fit it once, at the master end. The shield connects to enclosure
        ground at <b>one end only</b> — grounding both ends creates a ground loop that injects noise into
        the pair.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="note">
      <h3>Why only one terminator on this bus</h3>
      <p>Termination and fail-safe bias form one voltage divider, so they have to be chosen together.
         The idle differential voltage is</p>
      <p class="mono" style="color:var(--ink)">U_diff = 3.3 V × R_term / (2 × R_bias + R_term)</p>
      <p>An RS485 receiver needs more than <strong>200 mV</strong> to see a defined idle state:</p>
      <div class="tablewrap" style="margin:4px 0">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Configuration</th><th>R_term seen by the bias</th><th>U_diff idle</th><th></th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>2 × 120 Ω + 680 Ω bias</td><td>60 Ω (parallel)</td><td>139 mV</td><td>✗ below threshold</td></tr>
            <tr><td><b>1 × 120 Ω + 680 Ω bias</b></td><td>120 Ω</td><td><b>268 mV</b></td><td>✓ used here</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2 × 120 Ω + 390 Ω bias</td><td>60 Ω (parallel)</td><td>236 mV</td><td>✓ valid alternative</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p><strong>Why the second terminator is not needed anyway.</strong> At 9600 baud one bit lasts
         <strong>104 µs</strong>, while a reflection on a 2 m stub has settled after roughly <strong>20 ns</strong> —
         a ratio of about 1:5000. The receiver samples mid-bit, long after any ringing has died away.
         Termination matters on multi-megabit buses; on a few metres at 9600 baud it buys nothing and only
         drags the bias level down.</p>
      <p>So: <strong>do not add a terminator at the probes.</strong> If you ever raise the baud rate or extend
         the run substantially, fit the second 120 Ω <em>and</em> drop the bias resistors to ~390 Ω in the
         same step — never one without the other.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <section>
    <h2><span class="num">DRAWING 03</span>Power chain and protection</h2>
    <p>One battery domain, two output rails. The protection parts sit between the battery and everything
       else, so a surge coming down the solar cable or a reversed connector is stopped before it reaches
       the boost converter or the MCU.</p>

    <figure>
      <div class="canvas">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 330" role="img"
             aria-label="Power chain: solar panel through a TVS diode to the MPPT charge controller, then the 18650 battery, then a PTC fuse and SS34 Schottky diode with a TVS across the rail. The protected rail feeds the board directly at 3.7 volts and an XL6009 boost converter to 12 volts, which passes through a GPIO-controlled high-side switch and a 1000 microfarad bulk capacitor to the sensor rail.">
          <defs>
            <marker id="ar3" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="var(--rail12)"/>
            </marker>
          </defs>
          <g font-family="IBM Plex Mono, monospace" font-size="12" fill="currentColor">

            <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" fill="none">
              <rect x="16"  y="70" width="112" height="48" rx="2"/>
              <rect x="196" y="70" width="120" height="48" rx="2"/>
              <rect x="384" y="70" width="120" height="48" rx="2"/>
              <rect x="572" y="70" width="120" height="48" rx="2"/>
            </g>
            <text x="72"  y="90"  text-anchor="middle">Solar 6 V</text>
            <text x="72"  y="106" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">5–10 W</text>
            <text x="256" y="90"  text-anchor="middle">Charge ctrl</text>
            <text x="256" y="106" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">MPPT</text>
            <text x="444" y="90"  text-anchor="middle">Battery</text>
            <text x="444" y="106" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">18650 · 3.0–4.2 V</text>
            <text x="632" y="90"  text-anchor="middle">XL6009 boost</text>
            <text x="632" y="106" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">→ 12 V</text>

            <g stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="2.2" marker-end="url(#ar3)">
              <line x1="128" y1="94" x2="190" y2="94"/>
              <line x1="316" y1="94" x2="378" y2="94"/>
              <line x1="504" y1="94" x2="566" y2="94"/>
              <line x1="692" y1="94" x2="754" y2="94"/>
            </g>

            <!-- protection markers on the battery-to-boost run -->
            <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" fill="var(--surface)">
              <rect x="510" y="40" width="48" height="20" rx="2"/>
            </g>
            <text x="534" y="54" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10">PTC 2.6 A</text>
            <line x1="534" y1="60" x2="534" y2="94" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>

            <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" fill="var(--surface)">
              <rect x="470" y="150" width="52" height="20" rx="2"/>
              <rect x="540" y="150" width="60" height="20" rx="2"/>
            </g>
            <text x="496" y="164" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10">SS34</text>
            <text x="570" y="164" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10">SMBJ5.0A</text>
            <line x1="496" y1="150" x2="496" y2="94"  stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
            <line x1="570" y1="150" x2="570" y2="94"  stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
            <line x1="570" y1="170" x2="570" y2="266" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
            <text x="470" y="188" font-size="10" fill="var(--ink-3)">reverse-polarity · TVS clamp</text>

            <!-- TVS on solar input -->
            <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" fill="var(--surface)">
              <rect x="132" y="150" width="60" height="20" rx="2"/>
            </g>
            <text x="162" y="164" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10">TVS</text>
            <line x1="162" y1="150" x2="162" y2="94"  stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
            <line x1="162" y1="170" x2="162" y2="266" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>

            <!-- branch to board -->
            <path d="M 444 118 L 444 220 L 300 220" stroke="var(--rail33)" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/>
            <rect x="176" y="196" width="124" height="48" rx="2" fill="var(--surface-2)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3"/>
            <text x="238" y="216" text-anchor="middle">WaziSense</text>
            <text x="238" y="232" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">VIN · 3.3 V logic</text>
            <text x="330" y="212" fill="var(--rail33)" font-size="11">3.7 V</text>

            <!-- high-side switch -->
            <rect x="758" y="70" width="126" height="48" rx="2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" fill="none"/>
            <text x="821" y="90"  text-anchor="middle">High-side sw</text>
            <text x="821" y="106" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">P-MOSFET #2811</text>
            <path d="M 300 236 L 700 236 L 700 130 L 754 130 L 754 106 L 758 106"
                  stroke="var(--rail33)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="5 4" fill="none"/>
            <text x="430" y="252" fill="var(--rail33)" font-size="11">D6 gate (on-board MOSFET, boots OFF)</text>

            <!-- bulk cap + rail out -->
            <line x1="884" y1="94" x2="960" y2="94" stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="2.6"/>
            <g stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="2">
              <line x1="916" y1="94" x2="916" y2="120"/>
              <line x1="904" y1="120" x2="928" y2="120"/>
              <line x1="904" y1="127" x2="928" y2="127"/>
              <line x1="916" y1="127" x2="916" y2="266"/>
            </g>
            <text x="934" y="122" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="10">1000 µF</text>
            <text x="960" y="80" text-anchor="end" fill="var(--rail12)" font-size="11">+12 V rail →</text>

            <!-- ground -->
            <line x1="16" y1="266" x2="960" y2="266" stroke="var(--ink-3)" stroke-width="2.6"/>
            <g stroke="var(--ink-3)" stroke-width="1.4">
              <line x1="72"  y1="118" x2="72"  y2="266"/>
              <line x1="256" y1="118" x2="256" y2="266"/>
              <line x1="444" y1="118" x2="444" y2="196"/>
              <line x1="238" y1="244" x2="238" y2="266"/>
              <line x1="632" y1="118" x2="632" y2="266"/>
            </g>
            <text x="24" y="286" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">GND — continuous from battery to every probe; the switch is on the +12 V side only</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="legend">
        <span><i class="swatch sw12"></i>power path</span>
        <span><i class="swatch sw33"></i>3.3 V / control</span>
        <span><i class="swatch swg"></i>GND</span>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        The <b>PTC</b> is resettable, so an overcurrent event does not need a field visit to replace a fuse.
        The <b>SS34</b> costs about 0.5 V of forward drop in exchange for reverse-polarity immunity — an
        acceptable trade at this power level. Note the <b>gate pull-down</b>: without it the 12 V rail state
        is undefined between power-up and the first line of firmware.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <section>
    <h2><span class="num">TABLE 01</span>Pin assignment — WaziSense v2</h2>
    <p>Taken from the <em>WaziSense v2 Internal User Manual</em> and matching the constants at the top of
       <code>WaterSensorNode.ino</code>. <strong>D2, D9, D10, D11, D12, D13 belong to the RFM95W radio</strong> and
       are not available; I²C is fixed to A4/A5 in hardware.</p>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Pin</th><th>Sketch constant</th><th>Connects to</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>D3</code></td><td><code>RS485_RX_PIN</code></td><td>MAX3485 <code>RO</code></td><td>SoftwareSerial receive</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>D4</code></td><td><code>RS485_TX_PIN</code></td><td>MAX3485 <code>DI</code></td><td>SoftwareSerial transmit</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>D5</code></td><td><code>RS485_DE_PIN</code></td><td>MAX3485 <code>DE</code> + <code>RE</code> (tied)</td><td>HIGH = drive bus, LOW = listen</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>D6</code></td><td><code>SENSOR_RAIL_EN</code></td><td><b>"Sensor Power 1"</b> terminal block</td><td>On-board <b>high-side</b> MOSFET. H1 jumper selects BATT or 3.3 V at the terminal. No external gate pull-down needed.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>A1</code></td><td><code>MAX31865_CS</code></td><td>MAX31865 <code>CS</code></td><td>Analog pin driven as a digital output</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>A2</code></td><td><code>ONE_WIRE_PIN</code></td><td>DS18B20 <code>DQ</code></td><td>Needs an external 4.7 kΩ pull-up. Disabled by default.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>A0</code></td><td><code>batt_pin</code></td><td>— (on board)</td><td>On-board 2 × 470 kΩ divider. <code>BATT%</code> jumper can be cut to free A0.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>A4</code></td><td>— (<code>Wire</code>)</td><td>SDA → both EZO isolators</td><td><b>4.7 kΩ pull-up already fitted on the board</b> (<code>I2C_J</code>)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>A5</code></td><td>— (<code>Wire</code>)</td><td>SCL → both EZO isolators</td><td><b>4.7 kΩ pull-up already fitted on the board</b> (<code>I2C_J</code>)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>D8</code></td><td><code>ledPin</code></td><td>— (on board LED1)</td><td>Boot blink pattern</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>D11/12/13</code></td><td>— (<code>SPI</code>)</td><td>Radio <b>and</b> MAX31865</td><td>Shared bus; each device has its own CS</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>D2 · D9 · D10</code></td><td>—</td><td>RFM95W DIO0 · RESET · NSS</td><td><b>Reserved — do not use</b></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>D7 · A3</code></td><td>—</td><td>— free —</td><td>Spare: "Sensor Power 2" block, and one analog/digital pin</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="note">
      <h3>Three things the WaziSense manual changes</h3>
      <p><strong>1. The I²C pull-ups are already on the board.</strong> Two 4.7 kΩ resistors to 3.3 V, enabled by
         the <code>I2C_J</code> jumper (closed from the factory). <strong>Do not fit your own</strong> — in parallel they
         would give ~2.35 kΩ and overload the bus. Cut <code>I2C_J</code> only if you ever want A4/A5 as plain
         analog inputs.</p>
      <p><strong>2. D6 and D7 are ready-made high-side switches.</strong> The block diagram calls it a "Dedicated
         VCC Mosfet" — the positive line is switched and ground runs through, exactly the topology the RS485
         bus needs. With the <strong>H1 jumper on BATT</strong> the terminal carries battery voltage, so you can gate
         the XL6009's <em>input</em> from D6 and switch the converter's quiescent current off along with the
         sensors. <em>Open question: the on-board MOSFET's current rating — the battery side needs ~2 A. Read
         the part number off the board before relying on it; if it is too small, use D6 as the logic signal
         for the external 22 A module instead and keep that on the 12 V side.</em></p>
      <p><strong>3. Battery sensing is on-board.</strong> A0 sits on a 2 × 470 kΩ divider; you do not add your own.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <section>
    <h2><span class="num">TABLE 02</span>Bus addresses</h2>
    <p>Every device on a shared bus needs a unique address. The values below match the sketch —
       change either side to suit, but keep them in sync.</p>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Device</th><th>Bus</th><th>Address</th><th>Supply</th><th>Warm-up before read</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>PT1000 temperature</td><td><b>SPI</b> via MAX31865</td><td>CS on <code>A1</code></td><td>3.3 V (front-end)</td><td>immediate</td></tr>
          <tr><td>DO — DFRobot SEN0680</td><td>RS485</td><td><code>0x02</code></td><td>+12 V rail</td><td>~5 s (optics)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Turbidity — Y511-A</td><td>RS485</td><td><code>0x03</code></td><td>+12 V rail</td><td>~30 s (wiper sweep) — read every 4th cycle</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Atlas EZO-pH</td><td>I²C</td><td><code>0x63</code></td><td>3.3 V</td><td>900 ms per <code>R</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Atlas EZO-EC</td><td>I²C</td><td><code>0x64</code></td><td>3.3 V</td><td>900 ms per <code>R</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <section>
    <h2><span class="num">DRAWING 04</span>Protection — how PTC, SS34 and SMBJ connect</h2>
    <p>Two parts sit <strong>in series</strong> in the positive line, one sits <strong>in parallel</strong> across the
       rail. Polarity of the two diodes is the whole point — fit either one backwards and you get
       no output at all, or no protection at all.</p>

    <figure>
      <div class="canvas">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 920 400" role="img"
             aria-label="Protection schematic. From the battery positive terminal, a PTC fuse and then an SS34 Schottky diode are wired in series, the diode cathode facing away from the battery toward the load. At the output node an SMBJ5.0A transient voltage suppressor is wired in parallel to ground, with its cathode facing the positive rail. The battery negative connects directly to the ground rail.">
          <defs>
            <marker id="cur" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="var(--rail12)"/>
            </marker>
          </defs>
          <g font-family="IBM Plex Mono, monospace" font-size="12" fill="currentColor">

            <!-- ===== battery symbol ===== -->
            <g stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="2">
              <line x1="110" y1="110" x2="110" y2="165"/>
            </g>
            <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <line x1="90"  y1="165" x2="130" y2="165"/>
              <line x1="99"  y1="175" x2="121" y2="175"/>
              <line x1="90"  y1="185" x2="130" y2="185"/>
              <line x1="99"  y1="195" x2="121" y2="195"/>
            </g>
            <line x1="110" y1="195" x2="110" y2="300" stroke="var(--ink-3)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <text x="138" y="162" fill="var(--rail12)" font-size="14">+</text>
            <text x="138" y="200" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="14">−</text>
            <text x="110" y="240" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">Battery</text>
            <text x="110" y="256" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">3.0–4.2 V</text>

            <!-- ===== positive line ===== -->
            <g stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="2">
              <line x1="110" y1="110" x2="200" y2="110"/>
              <line x1="246" y1="110" x2="320" y2="110"/>
              <line x1="342" y1="110" x2="700" y2="110"/>
            </g>

            <!-- PTC symbol: resistor box with diagonal -->
            <rect x="200" y="99" width="46" height="22" rx="1" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <line x1="205" y1="117" x2="241" y2="103" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <text x="223" y="86" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12">PTC</text>
            <text x="223" y="142" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="10">2.6 A / 6 V</text>
            <text x="223" y="156" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="10">not polarised</text>

            <!-- SS34 diode symbol -->
            <polygon points="320,98 320,122 342,110" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"/>
            <line x1="342" y1="96" x2="342" y2="124" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4"/>
            <text x="331" y="84" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12">SS34</text>
            <text x="316" y="142" text-anchor="end" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="10">anode</text>
            <text x="348" y="142" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="10">cathode = printed ring</text>
            <text x="348" y="156" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="10">ring points AWAY from battery</text>

            <!-- current direction -->
            <line x1="420" y1="80" x2="500" y2="80" stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#cur)"/>
            <text x="460" y="70" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--rail12)" font-size="10">normal current flow</text>

            <!-- junction + output -->
            <circle cx="480" cy="110" r="4" fill="var(--rail12)"/>
            <circle cx="700" cy="110" r="5" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <text x="716" y="106" fill="var(--rail12)">+VBATT</text>
            <text x="716" y="124" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="10">→ X1-1 · boost IN+ · board VIN</text>

            <!-- ===== TVS shunt ===== -->
            <line x1="480" y1="110" x2="480" y2="192" stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <path d="M 464 182 L 464 192 L 496 192 L 496 202" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4"/>
            <polygon points="468,214 492,214 480,192" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"/>
            <line x1="480" y1="214" x2="480" y2="300" stroke="var(--ink-3)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <text x="512" y="188" font-size="12">SMBJ5.0A</text>
            <text x="512" y="204" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="10">cathode (ring) UP, to +</text>
            <text x="512" y="218" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="10">anode DOWN, to GND</text>
            <text x="512" y="232" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="10">reverse-biased = blocks normally</text>

            <!-- ===== ground rail ===== -->
            <line x1="110" y1="300" x2="700" y2="300" stroke="var(--ink-3)" stroke-width="2.6"/>
            <line x1="300" y1="300" x2="300" y2="322" stroke="var(--ink-3)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <g stroke="var(--ink-3)" stroke-width="2.2">
              <line x1="282" y1="322" x2="318" y2="322"/>
              <line x1="288" y1="329" x2="312" y2="329"/>
              <line x1="294" y1="336" x2="306" y2="336"/>
            </g>
            <text x="300" y="360" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="11">GND / X1-2</text>
            <text x="560" y="286" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="10">the negative line is never interrupted</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <b>Series</b> — PTC then SS34, in that order: the fuse closest to the energy source protects the diode
        behind it. <b>Parallel</b> — the SMBJ sits across the rail after the diode, so it clamps whatever reaches
        the boost converter and the MCU. If the SMBJ ever conducts hard, the PTC upstream trips, which is
        the intended chain of events.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="note">
      <h3>Getting the two diodes the right way round</h3>
      <p><strong>SS34 (series).</strong> The printed ring marks the cathode. It faces the <em>load</em>. Fitted
         backwards, nothing downstream powers up at all — an easy fault to spot. Test: with the battery
         connected the correct way, you should measure roughly battery voltage minus 0.5 V at
         <code>+VBATT</code>.</p>
      <p><strong>SMBJ5.0A (parallel).</strong> The ring marks the cathode and faces <em>+VBATT</em>. Fitted
         backwards it becomes a plain forward-biased diode across your battery — it will conduct
         immediately, get hot, and trip the PTC. Test: in circuit and un-powered, a diode-mode meter
         should read open from <code>+VBATT</code> to GND in one direction and a diode drop in the other.</p>
      <p><strong>PTC.</strong> Not polarised — fit it either way round.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <section>
    <h2><span class="num">DRAWING 05</span>Full power schematic</h2>
    <p>Discrete parts drawn as component symbols, ready-made modules as boxes with named pins. Every
       positive and negative conductor is drawn. <strong>Wires that cross without a filled dot are not
       connected</strong> — only a dot means a junction.</p>

    <figure>
      <div class="canvas">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 560" role="img"
             aria-label="Full power schematic in classic symbols. A photovoltaic panel feeds a charge controller with separate positive and negative wires, with a transient suppressor to ground on the positive line. The battery hangs between the positive node and ground. In series follow a PTC fuse and an SS34 diode to the VBATT rail, which carries a second transient suppressor to ground. VBATT feeds the WaziSense board and, on a lower branch, an XL6009 boost converter, a high-side switch controlled by pin D4 with a 100 kilohm pull-down, a 1000 microfarad capacitor, and the plus 12 volt switched rail. All negative conductors run to one ground rail.">
          <g font-family="IBM Plex Mono, monospace" font-size="11" fill="currentColor">

            <!-- ===== PV panel symbol ===== -->
            <rect x="40" y="68" width="78" height="58" rx="1" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1">
              <line x1="58"  y1="126" x2="78"  y2="68"/>
              <line x1="78"  y1="126" x2="98"  y2="68"/>
              <line x1="98"  y1="126" x2="118" y2="68"/>
            </g>
            <g stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="1.3">
              <line x1="18" y1="46" x2="40" y2="62"/>
              <line x1="36" y1="42" x2="54" y2="60"/>
            </g>
            <text x="79" y="146" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="10">Solar 6 V</text>

            <!-- PV to charge controller -->
            <line x1="118" y1="86"  x2="180" y2="86"  stroke="var(--rail12)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <line x1="118" y1="112" x2="180" y2="112" stroke="var(--ink-3)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <text x="132" y="80" fill="var(--rail12)" font-size="10">+</text>
            <text x="132" y="126" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="10">−</text>

            <rect x="180" y="68" width="118" height="58" rx="2" fill="var(--surface-2)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="239" y="92"  text-anchor="middle" font-size="11">Charge ctrl</text>
            <text x="239" y="108" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-3)" font-size="10">MPPT module</text>

